WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:05.920
When it comes to action movies, Underworld is the&nbsp;
gothic horror franchise that can't seem to rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:11.680
in peace. But if more sequels are on the way,&nbsp;
the series' leading lady won't be coming along.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:15.920
Let's take a look at why Kate Beckinsale&nbsp;
won't be back for more Underworld.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.720
As it crashed into cinemas at the tail&nbsp;
end of 2003's summer movie season,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.720
"Underworld" vividly re-imagined&nbsp;
what vampire fiction could be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:29.760
by positioning its blood-sucking beasts square&nbsp;
in the middle of a full-blown action epic.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:35.200
In the process, it made a legit action superstar&nbsp;
out of actress Kate Beckinsale. Perhaps more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.960
surprisingly, "Underworld" launched the vampires&nbsp;
vs. werewolves franchise the cinematic world never&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:46.320
knew it needed, and essentially put low-budget&nbsp;
genre studio Screen Gems on the Hollywood map.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:50.240
To date, Screen Gems and their partners&nbsp;
at Lakeshore Entertainment have produced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.680
three sequels and one prequel&nbsp;
for their flagship franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:58.320
and Kate Beckinsale has appeared as "Death&nbsp;
Dealer" Selene in every single one of them.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:01.600
The most recent "Underworld"&nbsp;
flick, subtitled "Blood Wars,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:07.280
hit theaters in 2016, and wasn't particularly&nbsp;
well received by either critics or audiences.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:10.720
That sort of performance rarely means&nbsp;
great things for a movie series, and to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.120
further complicate the "Underworld" producers'&nbsp;
potential dreams of Selene's future adventures,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:18.720
it appears that Beckinsale has joined the&nbsp;
ranks of people who don't want anything&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:22.880
to do with the franchise. In a 2018&nbsp;
Variety interview, the actress gave&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.920
some candid remarks about certain roles she'd&nbsp;
passed or, it turns out, had left behind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:32.240
When asked about the possibility of making&nbsp;
another "Underworld" movie, she was blunt.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.040
"I wouldn't return. I've done plenty of those."

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.640
Even by Hollywood standards,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:40.320
that curt response doesn't leave much&nbsp;
wiggle room for future appearances.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:47.360
"I have seen so much war. So&nbsp;
much killing. I can't bear more."

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:52.400
If you're among the few "Underworld" fans&nbsp;
who actually bought a ticket and experienced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:57.440
"Blood Wars" in theaters, you probably aren't too&nbsp;
heartbroken over Beckinsale's outright dismissal.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:02.400
After all, "Blood Wars" really was a bit of a&nbsp;
mess, and its less than enthusiastic reviews are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:07.200
enough to give an impression that the franchise&nbsp;
itself might feel a bit long in the fang.

00:02:07.200 --> 00:02:11.920
While Beckinsale didn't really address why she's&nbsp;
ready to move on from "Underworld" for good,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.920 --> 00:02:16.000
it's a reasonably safe bet that she's grown&nbsp;
as weary of the franchise's neo-gothic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.240
escapades as critics and viewers seem&nbsp;
to have. That's hardly a surprise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:23.600
given that the actor was never really&nbsp;
the blockbuster franchise sort.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:28.400
It's easy to forget, but Beckinsale actually&nbsp;
came up in showbiz on the strength of her work&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:33.600
in smaller-scaled projects like "Much Ado About&nbsp;
Nothing," "The Golden Bowl," and "Laurel Canyon."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.920
In the years since her "Underworld" breakout,&nbsp;
Beckinsale has continued to dip her toe in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.160
indie cinema pool every once in a while,&nbsp;
balancing these projects with larger-scale&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:48.000
fare like "Click." For instance, Beckinsale's 2016&nbsp;
reunion with her "The Last Days of Disco" director&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:52.960
Whit Stillman for the tragically underrated period&nbsp;
piece, "Love &amp; Friendship," earned rave reviews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.960 --> 00:02:58.080
... and came out the same year as "Underworld:&nbsp;
Blood Wars." Which career path would you choose?

00:02:58.080 --> 00:02:59.520
"Oh, I can't decide!"

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.360
Per a 2017 interview with Yahoo, while addressing&nbsp;
the rumors of her playing Wonder Woman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:09.520
Beckinsale acknowledged that part of why she&nbsp;
passed on the role was out of a desire not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.520
to appear in Princess Diana's famously&nbsp;
short-skirted outfit and embarrass her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.520 --> 00:03:17.920
daughter. In her statement, Beckinsale clearly&nbsp;
addressed her "Underworld" getup, as well.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:21.360
"I don't know if I was desperate&nbsp;
to be in a leotard. I'd already&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:24.160
done the rubber trousers. You&nbsp;
have to take in that you have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:27.440
a child at some point and how much&nbsp;
could you possibly embarrass them."

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.760
It would seem, then, that Kate Beckinsale wasn't&nbsp;
too keen on those "rubber trousers" throughout her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:31.760 --> 00:03:36.160
"Underworld" tenure. Whether or not the thought&nbsp;
of squeezing back into that skin-tight ensemble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.160 --> 00:03:40.960
another time fueled Beckinsale's decision to&nbsp;
leave the franchise for good remains a mystery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.600
but it sounds like the pants may&nbsp;
have factored into the process.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:48.560
Whatever the reason behind Beckinsale's&nbsp;
decision to leave the "Underworld" franchise is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.560 --> 00:03:53.520
one thing is certain: It definitely isn't&nbsp;
because she's feeling too old for action roles.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:58.720
In a 2020 interview with Women's Health, the then&nbsp;
46-year-old actress discussed her healthy diet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:04.640
her action star-worthy fitness regime and her&nbsp;
2021 Amazon Prime Video action movie, "Jolt."

00:04:04.640 --> 00:04:10.320
"'It can feel like a little bit of a political act&nbsp;
to be a woman over 32 who's having any fun at all.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:14.320
And by that, I don't mean doing drugs and&nbsp;
drinking and partying, because I never am,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:18.000
but being goofy, and going out&nbsp;
[...] it somehow seems to be risqué,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.000 --> 00:04:22.080
which is just ridiculous to me. And I witness&nbsp;
men constantly doing whatever they like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.080 --> 00:04:26.640
whether that's in relationships, or deciding&nbsp;
to buy a motorbike, or getting a tattoo."

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:30.800
Perhaps not entirely coincidentally,&nbsp;
"Jolt" turns this concept on its head.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:35.280
Beckinsale plays Lindy, a former bouncer&nbsp;
with violent impulse control issues.

00:04:35.280 --> 00:04:38.880
"I explain, 'It's this woman who's&nbsp;
got this rage disorder.' And every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:42.720
single woman has said, 'Oh. Me.' Women&nbsp;
are really f------- angry right now."

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.160
Kate Beckinsale's recent and upcoming&nbsp;
filmography makes her star-making role as Selene&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:52.400
seem like the odd one out in her résumé. The&nbsp;
actress seems to be building on the critical&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:57.280
success of "Love &amp; Friendship," and focusing on&nbsp;
projects like the coming-of-age drama "Farming,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.280 --> 00:05:00.560
and the Amazon Prime Original&nbsp;
mystery drama "The Widow."

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:03.200
According to Deadline, one of&nbsp;
Beckinsale's more interesting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.880
upcoming projects is director Catherine&nbsp;
Hardwicke's "Prisoner's Daughter," which&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.360
will be about generational family trauma and&nbsp;
the long road to healing. In other words,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.360 --> 00:05:15.440
it's going to be about as far from&nbsp;
vampire action movies as you can get.

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:19.840
Perhaps this is the ultimate reason Beckinsale&nbsp;
won't return for "Underworld 6:" She simply wants&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.840 --> 00:05:25.040
to star in projects like these instead. Beckinsale&nbsp;
clearly has much to give on the acting front,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.040 --> 00:05:30.640
and let's face it — five movies of stunts in&nbsp;
a skin-tight costume is plenty for anyone.

